@node Limitations
@chapter Limitations and roadmap

The feature set of the original library that matters for niori.el is
ported: the object model and writer, pure-Elisp DEFLATE, Base-14 fonts
with AFM metrics, kerning pairs and Symbol/ZapfDingbats native
encodings, TrueType subsetting, CFF/OTF embedding with CFF-level
subsetting, TrueType collections, Type 1 font embedding (.pfb/.pfa
with eexec/charstring width extraction), JPEG/PNG images,
the full vector graphics layer, document outlines, AcroForms, bar
codes, chart helpers, glyph outline drawing, PDF/A-2b archival
output, and a cl-typesetting style flow engine with Knuth-Plass line
breaking and TeX-pattern hyphenation.

A complete showcase is @file{examples/alice-book.el}, which typesets
Lewis Carroll's @emph{Alice's Adventures in Wonderland} as an 86-page
A5 book with serif body text, sans-serif headings, running heads, a
linked table of contents and a QR colophon - all from Elisp.

Remaining differences from the Common Lisp originals:

@itemize
@item Font features beyond cmap/glyf/CharStrings (hinting engines,
GSUB/GPOS shaping) are not used.
@item AcroForm JavaScript actions and digital signatures are out of
scope.
@item Hyphenation patterns ship for English (American and British),
German, French, Spanish (one set - the RAE/ASALE orthography is
common to all Spanish variants), Italian, Portuguese (one set for
pt-PT and pt-BR), Esperanto, Ukrainian and Russian.  Other languages
can be added with the same generator.
@end itemize

